1
00:00:51,468 --> 00:00:53,220
Hello, friend!

2
00:00:54,012 --> 00:00:56,014
You look like a...

3
00:00:56,390 --> 00:00:59,308
Professor Lee Huang the Third!

4
00:01:00,894 --> 00:01:03,145
Oh, Sang!

5
00:01:03,146 --> 00:01:04,605
That's lovely.

6
00:01:05,107 --> 00:01:06,482
My name's Pavi.

7
00:01:06,483 --> 00:01:08,276
And this here is Geet!

8
00:01:10,946 --> 00:01:14,449
Come on, Geet, let's
introduce him to the family!

9
00:01:54,656 --> 00:01:56,240
Agh! It's been decades.

10
00:01:56,241 --> 00:01:58,452
Could you just learn
one more song?

11
00:02:00,203 --> 00:02:02,497
I don't know,
that tune's pretty catchy!

12
00:02:02,956 --> 00:02:04,707
You're not helping, Jae!

13
00:02:13,550 --> 00:02:14,885
Wall integrity? Dense.

14
00:02:15,010 --> 00:02:16,261
Storm gutters? Clean.

15
00:02:16,386 --> 00:02:18,013
Checklist? Checked.

16
00:02:30,233 --> 00:02:32,318
What's up, big guy?

17
00:02:32,319 --> 00:02:34,404
See you at the festival, Jae!

18
00:02:38,700 --> 00:02:40,410
Hmm?

19
00:02:41,119 --> 00:02:43,287
- Hey, Jae!
- Hey, everyone!

20
00:02:43,288 --> 00:02:45,207
- What's up, Jae?
- How's it going, Jae?

21
00:02:46,792 --> 00:02:48,501
Save some mochi for me, Lulu!

22
00:02:48,502 --> 00:02:51,253
I'll save five sticks
just for you.

23
00:02:51,254 --> 00:02:52,214
Love you.

24
00:03:02,140 --> 00:03:04,017
Geet, no chompies.

25
00:03:06,061 --> 00:03:07,145
Is that Jae?

26
00:03:07,270 --> 00:03:08,896
Up for a game
of Pai Sho, Jae?

27
00:03:08,897 --> 00:03:10,272
I thought you were sick
of losing!

28
00:03:10,273 --> 00:03:13,235
What's up, Jae?

29
00:03:20,951 --> 00:03:23,036
I'm telling you,
that rattle-raven

30
00:03:23,161 --> 00:03:24,830
almost bit a chunk
out of my ear!

31
00:03:24,955 --> 00:03:27,206
Well, you did try to take
his dead rat.

32
00:03:27,207 --> 00:03:28,874
Hey, Uki! Hey, Lan.

33
00:03:28,875 --> 00:03:30,460
- Oh. Hi, Jae!
- Hi, Jae!

34
00:03:30,877 --> 00:03:32,546
- Jae, my friend!
- Daemin!

35
00:03:32,671 --> 00:03:35,298
What did we say about
surprise hugs, buddy?

36
00:03:36,049 --> 00:03:38,260
Only on my birthday...

37
00:03:38,385 --> 00:03:41,345
Let's head to the festival
and grab some lotus fritters.

38
00:03:41,346 --> 00:03:43,597
We could do something
even more fun.

39
00:03:43,598 --> 00:03:45,933
Patrolling for danger!

40
00:03:45,934 --> 00:03:47,935
Hmph.

41
00:03:47,936 --> 00:03:49,729
Come on, guys.

42
00:03:49,730 --> 00:03:52,565
As squad leader,
you gotta listen to me.

43
00:03:52,566 --> 00:03:53,899
He did it.

44
00:03:53,900 --> 00:03:55,694
Jae played
the squad leader card!

45
00:03:56,069 --> 00:03:58,947
I think I'd like to see
this so-called "card."

46
00:04:00,907 --> 00:04:02,116
- Watch out!
- Huh?

47
00:04:25,098 --> 00:04:27,434
- Mwah!
- Great job, squad.

48
00:04:27,851 --> 00:04:30,102
Now we definitely deserve
lotus fritters!

49
00:04:30,103 --> 00:04:32,147
Nope!
Back to the bending compound.

50
00:04:32,272 --> 00:04:33,189
Aww.

51
00:04:33,190 --> 00:04:35,108
Ah! Squad Leader card!

52
00:04:40,030 --> 00:04:42,448
Hey, squad leader,
lead already!

53
00:04:42,449 --> 00:04:44,618
Yeah, yeah, let's go.

54
00:04:49,956 --> 00:04:51,958
Geet, we've talked about this.

55
00:04:52,083 --> 00:04:53,125
Stealth.

56
00:04:53,126 --> 00:04:55,670
You have cat-monkey-like
reflexes!

57
00:04:55,796 --> 00:04:56,880
Use them!

58
00:04:59,007 --> 00:05:00,592
Of course I forgive you.

59
00:05:01,092 --> 00:05:02,803
Did you find anything good
in there?

60
00:05:04,805 --> 00:05:07,182
Ugh! Mudpies, nothing!

61
00:05:18,318 --> 00:05:20,945
It's too bad that customer
didn't want

62
00:05:20,946 --> 00:05:24,199
these fresh, delicious kachoris.

63
00:05:24,324 --> 00:05:26,159
I guess I'm just gonna have
to throw them out!

64
00:05:50,809 --> 00:05:52,017
Welcome home, Sang!

65
00:05:53,395 --> 00:05:54,521
Meet the family.

66
00:06:12,539 --> 00:06:14,040
You, and you, and...

67
00:06:14,165 --> 00:06:16,126
You're allergic! ...and you.

68
00:06:21,882 --> 00:06:23,466
Sang, what's wrong?

69
00:06:31,808 --> 00:06:32,766
I know.

70
00:06:32,767 --> 00:06:34,394
This isn't your real home.

71
00:06:34,519 --> 00:06:36,479
Sang needs his family, Geet.

72
00:06:36,605 --> 00:06:39,940
You know that family's
the most important thing.

73
00:06:43,528 --> 00:06:46,489
Okay, Sang, let's go find
your mom and dad.

74
00:06:58,209 --> 00:06:59,919
Sorry! Your hole is lovely!

75
00:06:59,920 --> 00:07:02,129
The Brigade!

76
00:07:02,130 --> 00:07:03,214
We gotta hide!

77
00:07:12,515 --> 00:07:14,183
This is Commander Bountan.

78
00:07:14,184 --> 00:07:15,185
Open up!

79
00:07:16,227 --> 00:07:18,313
No! I won't let you take him.

80
00:07:18,772 --> 00:07:20,106
I know this is hard,

81
00:07:20,231 --> 00:07:23,609
but the law states every bender
must join the Brigade.

82
00:07:23,610 --> 00:07:24,611
Our haven needs--

83
00:07:24,736 --> 00:07:26,029
I don't care
what the haven needs.

84
00:07:26,154 --> 00:07:27,196
He's my son.

85
00:07:27,197 --> 00:07:29,574
Oh, man,
it's the Human Hurricane!

86
00:07:29,699 --> 00:07:30,617
The Warrior of the Wind!

87
00:07:30,742 --> 00:07:32,535
Master of the Tornado Fist.

88
00:07:32,661 --> 00:07:35,205
Captain Karthik is fine.

89
00:07:35,664 --> 00:07:36,914
Ulan, stop!

90
00:07:36,915 --> 00:07:38,291
You're not ready.

91
00:07:39,668 --> 00:07:41,962
Malika,
what's Ellora's motto?

92
00:07:44,297 --> 00:07:46,466
"For the survival of Ellora."

93
00:07:46,591 --> 00:07:47,467
Exactly.

94
00:07:48,051 --> 00:07:51,054
Your son isn't making
the biggest sacrifice, Malika.

95
00:07:51,596 --> 00:07:52,888
You are.

96
00:07:52,889 --> 00:07:53,890
Me?

97
00:07:54,641 --> 00:07:56,101
I'm just his mother.

98
00:07:56,893 --> 00:07:59,062
With the Brigade's ranks
shrinking each year,

99
00:07:59,187 --> 00:08:01,940
there's no greater gift
a mother can give than this.

100
00:08:02,565 --> 00:08:04,442
It's because of families
like yours

101
00:08:04,567 --> 00:08:06,361
our haven stands strong.

102
00:08:07,153 --> 00:08:10,239
You are not losing a child,
Malika.

103
00:08:10,240 --> 00:08:13,201
Ellora is gaining a hero...

104
00:08:14,202 --> 00:08:15,285
thanks to you.

105
00:08:21,418 --> 00:08:24,212
Listen to your captain,
keep your uniform clean,

106
00:08:24,337 --> 00:08:26,172
and make sure you eat breakfast.

107
00:08:26,297 --> 00:08:27,840
I know you'll make me proud.

108
00:08:33,638 --> 00:08:36,889
Trust me, the last thing we want
is to be noticed

109
00:08:36,890 --> 00:08:38,933
by anyone in the Brigade.

110
00:08:58,079 --> 00:09:00,622
There must be something
that hasn't been assigned.

111
00:09:00,623 --> 00:09:01,957
We'll even do cleaning duty!

112
00:09:01,958 --> 00:09:03,000
- No, we won't!
- Boo!

113
00:09:03,001 --> 00:09:04,461
Stop talking, Jae!

114
00:09:04,586 --> 00:09:06,378
Everything's covered
for the festival.

115
00:09:06,379 --> 00:09:08,630
If you finished your checks,
you're off duty.

116
00:09:08,631 --> 00:09:10,133
Why is no one else
in the Brigade

117
00:09:10,258 --> 00:09:11,925
taking today seriously?!

118
00:09:11,926 --> 00:09:14,804
- What's so special about today?
- Captain Karthik!

119
00:09:15,805 --> 00:09:16,765
Well...

120
00:09:17,057 --> 00:09:18,141
I mean...

121
00:09:18,266 --> 00:09:19,309
Today is...

122
00:09:19,976 --> 00:09:21,811
Ellora needs to be prepared,

123
00:09:22,145 --> 00:09:24,813
because long ago,
our ancestors weren't,

124
00:09:24,814 --> 00:09:26,733
and the Avatar let us down.

125
00:09:28,610 --> 00:09:31,154
Trust me, Jae, the Avatar
is not a threat today.

126
00:09:32,739 --> 00:09:35,449
In other words,
go get some fritters.

127
00:09:35,450 --> 00:09:36,451
That's an order.

128
00:09:37,243 --> 00:09:38,244
- Yes!
- Alright!

129
00:09:42,290 --> 00:09:43,625
I'm glad you're gone.

130
00:09:44,167 --> 00:09:46,336
<i>You can't hurt us anymore.</i>

131
00:09:49,756 --> 00:09:52,967
Hmph! Come here,
you little rascals!

132
00:09:54,260 --> 00:09:55,427
I got ya!

133
00:09:55,428 --> 00:09:58,348
You're gonna help me buy
a new scooter!

134
00:10:01,559 --> 00:10:04,186
Geet, we found Sang's family!

135
00:10:04,187 --> 00:10:05,938
Come on!
We gotta follow that kid.

136
00:10:19,619 --> 00:10:20,870
I know this is risky,

137
00:10:20,995 --> 00:10:22,579
but we'll be in and out.

138
00:10:22,580 --> 00:10:25,208
Sneaky like toad-mice. Promise!

139
00:10:25,333 --> 00:10:28,252
Rawr. I'm Avatar Korra,

140
00:10:28,253 --> 00:10:31,046
here to wreak havoc
on your lives.

141
00:10:34,676 --> 00:10:38,303
You can burn our home,
destroy our city,

142
00:10:38,304 --> 00:10:41,349
but you cannot break our spirit!

143
00:10:41,933 --> 00:10:43,142
Earth!

144
00:10:43,143 --> 00:10:44,309
Water!

145
00:10:44,310 --> 00:10:45,519
Air!

146
00:10:45,520 --> 00:10:46,937
Fire!

147
00:10:49,566 --> 00:10:50,900
Oh, no!

148
00:10:51,025 --> 00:10:53,318
I am vanquished!

149
00:10:54,404 --> 00:10:56,405
Hit her again!

150
00:10:57,407 --> 00:10:59,450
Get your
Anti-Avatar charms

151
00:10:59,576 --> 00:11:00,743
right here!

152
00:11:05,456 --> 00:11:07,667
She's selling your family?!

153
00:11:07,792 --> 00:11:10,628
Everyone knows
you can't put a price on a bug!

154
00:11:12,172 --> 00:11:16,759
So the Avatar's cruel reign
over humanity finally ended.

155
00:11:16,885 --> 00:11:20,304
Yet the Cataclysm
left our world in ruins.

156
00:11:20,305 --> 00:11:24,017
Our ancestors banded together
and created...

157
00:11:24,142 --> 00:11:25,977
the Seven Havens.

158
00:11:26,102 --> 00:11:28,688
Out from the rubble and chaos,

159
00:11:28,813 --> 00:11:31,940
we became our own heroes.

160
00:11:31,941 --> 00:11:33,775
Each haven found
its own unique way

161
00:11:33,776 --> 00:11:36,904
to let humanity thrive
once more.

162
00:11:36,905 --> 00:11:39,240
And Ellora's the best one!

163
00:11:39,365 --> 00:11:42,367
Does an Elloran cower
from a storm?

164
00:11:42,368 --> 00:11:44,203
- Never!
- A little bit!

165
00:11:44,204 --> 00:11:45,914
Against all odds,

166
00:11:46,039 --> 00:11:49,124
who built the haven
of wind and sand?!

167
00:11:49,125 --> 00:11:50,626
We did!

168
00:11:50,627 --> 00:11:51,960
What do we say?!

169
00:11:51,961 --> 00:11:54,422
For the survival of Ellora!

170
00:11:54,547 --> 00:11:57,216
I bet I could've taken
Avatar Korra on.

171
00:11:57,217 --> 00:11:59,718
No apocalypse
would've gone down on my watch.

172
00:11:59,719 --> 00:12:02,304
I wonder if the Avatar
was just cranky.

173
00:12:02,305 --> 00:12:04,181
You know?
Like, maybe she just needed

174
00:12:04,182 --> 00:12:05,516
her morning chai.

175
00:12:05,642 --> 00:12:06,725
Aw, Daemin.

176
00:12:06,726 --> 00:12:08,519
You remind me
of a hamster-puppy.

177
00:12:08,645 --> 00:12:11,897
That's the nicest thing
anyone's ever said about me!

178
00:12:13,650 --> 00:12:15,234
Hey, we shouldn't make light
of someone

179
00:12:15,235 --> 00:12:16,945
who caused so much destruction.

180
00:12:17,278 --> 00:12:18,737
Can you imagine
living in a world

181
00:12:18,738 --> 00:12:20,573
where the Avatar is in charge?

182
00:12:21,282 --> 00:12:22,574
I'd rather not.

183
00:12:22,575 --> 00:12:25,453
This play is already
giving me nightmares.

184
00:12:25,578 --> 00:12:26,703
Lan, it's okay.

185
00:12:26,704 --> 00:12:28,331
They're just actors.

186
00:12:28,456 --> 00:12:30,416
It's not real.

187
00:12:31,751 --> 00:12:34,087
- Hey!
- You can't sell those beetles!

188
00:12:34,212 --> 00:12:36,339
They're Sang's brothers
and sisters!

189
00:12:36,464 --> 00:12:37,465
Who's Sang?

190
00:12:37,590 --> 00:12:40,510
And who's gonna stop me,
the bug police?

191
00:12:42,136 --> 00:12:43,679
Let go of them!

192
00:12:43,680 --> 00:12:46,307
They deserve to be free
with their family...

193
00:12:46,432 --> 00:12:48,767
...and not some tacky jewelry!

194
00:12:48,768 --> 00:12:50,979
Who you calling tacky,
Goggle Girl?!

195
00:12:51,104 --> 00:12:53,689
I look small,
but I bite really hard.

196
00:12:53,690 --> 00:12:55,275
Let go of my bag!

197
00:12:56,317 --> 00:12:57,443
Ow!

198
00:13:04,492 --> 00:13:06,576
- Everything's under control.
- It's okay, everyone.

199
00:13:06,577 --> 00:13:09,037
Everyone, please stay calm!

200
00:13:09,038 --> 00:13:10,873
There's no need to pa--

201
00:13:14,961 --> 00:13:17,130
Get your bug spray! Going fast!

202
00:13:20,800 --> 00:13:22,635
She looks familiar...

203
00:13:23,219 --> 00:13:24,220
Sang...

204
00:13:24,971 --> 00:13:26,222
where did you go?

205
00:13:26,848 --> 00:13:27,848
Sang?

206
00:13:41,112 --> 00:13:43,822
See you at the family reunion,
Sang!

207
00:13:43,823 --> 00:13:45,366
She's not part of the Brigade...

208
00:13:45,491 --> 00:13:47,952
That's an unregistered bender!

209
00:13:48,745 --> 00:13:49,537
Hey!

210
00:13:49,662 --> 00:13:50,830
L-Little earthbender!

211
00:13:54,542 --> 00:13:56,126
Hey! Come back!

212
00:13:56,127 --> 00:13:58,338
Better her than me.

213
00:14:28,701 --> 00:14:30,536
Wait up, little earthbender!

214
00:14:34,665 --> 00:14:37,042
Check it out!
Jae just chased that girl out

215
00:14:37,043 --> 00:14:38,252
into the Harshlands.

216
00:14:38,878 --> 00:14:40,128
Is that a thing now?

217
00:14:40,129 --> 00:14:41,546
Instead of helping people,

218
00:14:41,547 --> 00:14:44,175
are we supposed to drive them
to their doom?

219
00:14:44,592 --> 00:14:47,470
Ugh. I hate
when they change up protocol.

220
00:15:11,994 --> 00:15:14,038
Ugh!

221
00:15:14,163 --> 00:15:16,332
We need to find shelter!

222
00:15:34,392 --> 00:15:36,185
Little earthbender?

223
00:15:36,602 --> 00:15:37,979
That sandstorm's getting worse!

224
00:15:38,104 --> 00:15:40,815
I need to get you back
to Ellora, where it's safe!

225
00:15:41,315 --> 00:15:43,484
That's a very special ability
you have.

226
00:15:43,985 --> 00:15:48,030
Did you know that there are
fewer benders born every year?

227
00:15:53,828 --> 00:15:56,747
I won't tell a soul about you,
I promise.

228
00:15:57,290 --> 00:15:58,541
Let's just go home.

229
00:16:00,084 --> 00:16:02,920
I understand how hard it can be
to trust people,

230
00:16:03,629 --> 00:16:05,840
especially if you've
just met them.

231
00:16:07,091 --> 00:16:07,884
I'm Jae!

232
00:16:08,426 --> 00:16:10,720
My favorite meal
is <i>kimchi chigae.</i>

233
00:16:11,137 --> 00:16:12,722
Um, I-I can juggle.

234
00:16:13,306 --> 00:16:15,057
Ah, I don't know how to whistle.

235
00:16:15,183 --> 00:16:18,519
Um, I-I don't like
scratchy scarves. Um...

236
00:16:19,145 --> 00:16:20,480
But most importantly,

237
00:16:21,147 --> 00:16:22,982
I don't make promises
I can't keep.

238
00:16:23,649 --> 00:16:26,027
We go back to Ellora
and you'll walk one way,

239
00:16:26,152 --> 00:16:27,403
and I'll walk the other.

240
00:16:27,820 --> 00:16:28,863
That's it.

241
00:16:56,599 --> 00:16:58,016
Geet, take cover!

242
00:16:58,017 --> 00:17:00,853
I know this is a bad idea!

243
00:17:22,708 --> 00:17:23,792
Ahh!

244
00:17:23,917 --> 00:17:26,295
Little earthbender!

245
00:17:33,135 --> 00:17:34,052
Look out!

246
00:17:52,363 --> 00:17:54,156
You can airbend?!

247
00:17:54,907 --> 00:17:55,950
The Avatar.

248
00:18:55,134 --> 00:18:57,720
She'll be okay.
She's just exhausted.

249
00:18:58,095 --> 00:19:00,765
I need to take her
somewhere she can get help.

250
00:19:13,235 --> 00:19:14,111
Jae?

251
00:19:14,236 --> 00:19:15,571
I thought I ordered you

252
00:19:15,696 --> 00:19:16,821
to enjoy the festival.

253
00:19:16,822 --> 00:19:19,283
I have a question and...

254
00:19:19,950 --> 00:19:22,536
and I don't trust anyone else
to answer it.

255
00:19:22,912 --> 00:19:23,913
I’m listening.

256
00:19:24,580 --> 00:19:28,833
The Avatar is the only being
who can bend multiple elements,

257
00:19:28,834 --> 00:19:29,752
right?

258
00:19:30,419 --> 00:19:34,590
Yes, multiple bending is a gift
solely reserved for the Avatar.

259
00:19:35,174 --> 00:19:38,052
Jae, why are you asking me
about ancient history?

260
00:19:39,011 --> 00:19:40,679
Ugh! Like everyone else,

261
00:19:40,680 --> 00:19:42,347
I believed that
if the Avatar came back,

262
00:19:42,348 --> 00:19:44,349
there would be bloodshed
and destruction.

263
00:19:44,350 --> 00:19:45,393
But now...

264
00:19:46,060 --> 00:19:47,310
I don't know.

265
00:19:47,311 --> 00:19:49,396
If I tell you what I saw,
you'll lock me up

266
00:19:49,397 --> 00:19:50,689
and throw away the key.

267
00:19:50,690 --> 00:19:52,608
What did you see?

268
00:19:55,236 --> 00:19:56,195
Jae,

269
00:19:56,612 --> 00:19:58,197
you can trust me.

270
00:19:59,365 --> 00:20:00,950
I have to show you something.

271
00:20:15,840 --> 00:20:17,299
Where did you find this girl?!

272
00:20:17,717 --> 00:20:20,302
I-I saw her
at the festival! Why?

273
00:20:20,428 --> 00:20:21,804
Do you know who she is?

274
00:20:21,929 --> 00:20:24,556
Tell me <i>exactly</i> how you met her.

275
00:20:27,268 --> 00:20:29,060
I chased her out
into the Harshlands

276
00:20:29,061 --> 00:20:31,439
and we got lost
in the Old World ruins.

277
00:20:31,856 --> 00:20:33,940
A tornado touched down and...

278
00:20:33,941 --> 00:20:35,567
- Shh!
- ...she saved us

279
00:20:35,568 --> 00:20:37,319
by bending earth...

280
00:20:37,445 --> 00:20:38,779
and air.

281
00:20:41,198 --> 00:20:42,992
You're sure that's what you saw?

282
00:20:43,409 --> 00:20:46,746
Sir, you can trust me
just like I trust you.

283
00:20:52,501 --> 00:20:53,794
Geet, this way!

284
00:20:59,592 --> 00:21:04,053
<i>Humanity is not ready
for the Avatar's return.</i>

285
00:21:04,054 --> 00:21:05,389
<i>And yet...</i>

286
00:21:05,973 --> 00:21:08,976
<i>it's the one thing
this world needs the most.</i>

287
00:21:09,477 --> 00:21:11,103
<i>Sir, I don't understand.</i>

288
00:21:11,228 --> 00:21:14,189
<i>The Avatar was humanity's
greatest curse.</i>

289
00:21:14,190 --> 00:21:15,691
<i>Not always.</i>

290
00:21:28,287 --> 00:21:29,288
You made a mistake.

291
00:21:29,872 --> 00:21:31,999
There's no way you could have
found the Avatar.

292
00:21:32,458 --> 00:21:35,710
Why not? How else
can you explain what I saw?

293
00:21:37,838 --> 00:21:40,466
You can't have found the Avatar
because...

294
00:21:42,510 --> 00:21:44,053
<i>I already have.</i>

